    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0580" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.01 Commuters/16</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of Labor</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Carr</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1927</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Carr</hi>: Enclosed find copy of General
                    Order No. 86, outlining land border crossing procedure, which may be of interest
                    to your Department, particularly, as it may greatly increase the applications
                    for non-quota visas at some of your consulates. I am informed this phase of the
                    question was discussed with you several weeks ago by Mr. Husband.<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d360-f1"/></p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robe Carl White</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d360-a1.xml" xpointer="d360-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
